.TH MONGOOSE-SOCKETCAN 1 "September 2026" "mongoose-j2534 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mongoose-socketcan \- bridge the MongoosePro adapter to a Linux CAN interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mongoose-socketcan
[\fB\-\-device\fR \fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-bitrate\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-29bit\fR]
[\fB\-\-transmit\fR]
[\fB\-\-stats\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
.I IFNAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mongoose-socketcan
opens a raw CAN channel on the adapter with a filter that passes every frame, and writes each frame it receives to
the SocketCAN interface
.IR IFNAME ,
normally a
.B vcan
interface made for it. Programs that speak SocketCAN, such as
.BR candump (1),
Wireshark, python-can, udsoncan and the kernel's
.B CAN_ISOTP
sockets, can then use the vehicle's bus without knowing about the adapter.
.PP
Frames that other programs write to
.I IFNAME
are sent to the vehicle only with
.BR \-\-transmit .
Without it the bridge is listen-only: nothing reaches the vehicle, and such frames are counted as refused. Remote
(RTR) and error frames are always refused, because J2534 cannot carry them.
.PP
It is an ordinary client of
.BR libmongoose_j2534 (7),
so only one program can use the adapter while it runs.
.PP
.B Use it at your own risk.
With
.BR \-\-transmit ,
anything any program writes to the interface goes onto the vehicle's bus.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " NAME"
The J2534 open name:
.BI serial: S\fR,
.BI tty: /dev/ttyACMn\fR,
and so on. The default is the one connected adapter.
.TP
.BI \-\-bitrate " N"
The vehicle bus rate, 500000 by default. Only the standard CAN rates are accepted. A wrong rate on a live bus is not
harmless.
.TP
.B \-\-29bit
Open the channel for 29-bit identifiers. A transmit may use either width regardless.
.TP
.B \-\-transmit
Send frames written to the interface onto the vehicle bus.
.TP
.BI \-\-stats " SECONDS"
Every
.I SECONDS
print frame counts to standard error: frames from the vehicle, frames to it, refused frames, adapter overflows (the
host fell behind and frames were lost), and frames the interface would not take.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo modprobe \-a vcan can\-isotp
sudo ip link add dev mongoose0 type vcan
sudo ip link set mongoose0 up
mongoose\-socketcan \-\-stats 10 mongoose0
candump \-ta mongoose0
.fi
.SS Starting it with systemd
An installed
.B mongoose-socketcan@.service
creates the interface named by the instance and runs the bridge on it, listen-only:
.PP
.nf
sudo systemctl start mongoose\-socketcan@mongoose0
.fi
.PP
Add
.B enable
to start it at boot, or
.B systemctl edit
it to add
.BR \-\-transmit .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after SIGINT or SIGTERM; 1 if the interface or the adapter could not be opened, or the adapter was lost while
running; 2 for a bad command line.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmongoose_j2534 (7),
.BR mongoose-client (1),
.BR mongoose-diag (1),
.BR candump (1).
The guide
.I docs/VOLVO.md
walks through the setup and reading data with Python.
